  "question": {
    "text": "If the bond dissociation energies of $X Y, X_2$ and $Y_2$ (all diatomic molecules) are in the ratio of 1:1:0.5 and $\\Delta_t \\mathrm{H}$ for the formation of $X Y$ is $-200 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mole}^{-1}$. The bond dissociation energy of $\\mathrm{X}_2$ will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$100 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$200 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$300 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nNone of these",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& X Y \\longrightarrow X_{(g)}+Y_{(g)} ; \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=+\\mathrm{a} \\mathrm{kJ} / \\mathrm{mole} \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots . .(\\mathrm{i}) \\\\\n& \\mathrm{X}_2 \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{X} ; \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=+\\mathrm{a} \\mathrm{kJ} / \\mathrm{mole} \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\text { (ii) } \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Y}_2 \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{Y} ; \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=+0.5 \\mathrm{a} \\mathrm{kJ} / \\mathrm{mole} \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots . \\text { (iii) } \\\\\n& \\frac{1}{2} \\times\\left. \\text { (ii) }+\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text { (iii) }-\\right.\\text { (i), Gives } \\\\\n& \\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{X}_2+\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{Y}_2 \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{XY} ; \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=\\left(+\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{2}+\\frac{0.5}{2} \\mathrm{a}-\\mathrm{a}\\right) \\mathrm{kJ} / \\mathrm{mole} \\\\\n& +\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{2}+\\frac{0.5 \\mathrm{a}}{2}-\\mathrm{a}=-200 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{a}=800 .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
